<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">New Braunfels</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/braunfels">Braunfels</a> is a city in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a>, between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-antonio">San Antonio</a> and Austin, on the Comal and Guadalupe rivers. It was founded in 1845 by German settlers of the Adelsverein led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-carl-of-solms-braunfels">Prince Carl of Solms-Braunfels</a> and named after Braunfels in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a>. It kept a strong German character and is known for its Wurstfest and river recreation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/new-braunfels.jpg" alt="New Braunfels" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Billy Hathorn at English Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Guadalupe_River_of_Texas_IMG_0500.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
